00:11:52,261 --> 00:11:54,380
or 200,000 amps of current,

207
00:11:54,381 --> 00:12:00,140
DNB's simulator provides invaluable data to those who create lightning countermeasures.

208
00:12:00,141 --> 00:12:07,760
That includes the makers of this seemingly simple tape, the most effective means to protect

209
00:12:07,761 --> 00:12:10,420
a plane's eyes and ears, its radar.

210
00:12:10,421 --> 00:12:15,995
What we want to do is intercept those lightning strikes.

211
00:12:15,996 --> 00:12:19,380
We place our device on the surface

212
00:12:19,381 --> 00:12:24,720
of the radome, and we place them around the antenna that's inside.

213
00:12:26,260 --> 00:12:29,000
When the lightning's initial electric charge hits,

214
00:12:29,460 --> 00:12:32,240
